  "Born Thornton Niven Wilder in Madison, Wisconsin, on 17 April 1897; his family lived in China, and he taught at Chicago and Harvard. The Bridge of San Luis Rey (1927) won the Pulitzer Prize, and Our Town (1938) and The Skin of Our Teeth (1942) made him the central American playwright of the period. He died in Hamden, Connecticut, on 7 December 1975.",
  "Thornton Wilder was the only writer to win Pulitzer Prizes for both fiction and drama: Our Town created the modern American theatre of the bare stage and The Bridge of San Luis Rey one of the great American novels of the century, and his humanism shaped the American stage for a generation.",
