  "Born Upton Beall Sinclair Jr in Baltimore on 20 September 1878; he wrote pulp fiction to pay for his education, joined the Socialist Party, and published The Jungle in 1906. King Coal (1917), Oil! (1927), Boston (1928) and the eleven Lanny Budd novels followed, and he won the Pulitzer Prize in 1943. He died in Bound Brook, New Jersey, on 25 November 1968.",
